<title>INDIA: India's forex reserves rise to $23.5 bln on Oct 25.</title>
<headline>India's forex reserves rise to $23.5 bln on Oct 25.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.5 billion on October 25, 1996, from $23.27 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Oct 25	Oct 18	 Oct 27</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,015	18,839	 18,219</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,410	 4,410	  4,405</p>
<p>    SDRs				    75	    18	     39</p>
<p>    Total			     23,500	23,267	 22,663</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
